+- AppShell wraps its keyed ChatWindow in a presentation-only boundary keyed by the same `sessionKey`. Keep all navigation, URL and agent ownership in AppShell; no new AgentSession or history cache is introduced.
+- On a changed key, retain the last committed child for an 80 ms opacity-only exit (1 → 0.55). The outgoing subtree is `inert`, so the old composer cannot submit under the new selection. One timer reads the latest props: rapid navigation never queues stale destinations; returning to the displayed key or unmounting cancels it. Updates under the same key keep the current children without remounting.
+- `app/conversation-transition.css` gives the incoming `.chat-content` one 180 ms entrance (0.55 → 1). ChatWindow mounts it only after loading, so a slow history request cannot consume the entrance on a placeholder. No translation, scale, blur or repeated breathing of the transcript. Reduced motion skips both the exit delay and CSS animation.
